    /// <p>QObject is the heart of the Qt <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/object.html">Object Model</a>. The central feature in this model is a very powerful mechanism for seamless object communication called <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/signalsandslots.html">signals and slots</a>. You can connect a signal to a slot with <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qobject.html#connect" translate="no">connect</a>() and destroy the connection with <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qobject.html#disconnect" translate="no">disconnect</a>(). To avoid never ending notification loops you can temporarily block signals with <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qobject.html#blockSignals" translate="no">blockSignals</a>(). The protected functions <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qobject.html#connectNotify" translate="no">connectNotify</a>() and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qobject.html#disconnectNotify" translate="no">disconnectNotify</a>() make it possible to track connections.</p>
