    /// <p>A guarded pointer, QPointer&lt;T&gt;, behaves like a normal C++ pointer <code translate="no">T *</code>, except that it is automatically cleared when the referenced object is destroyed (unlike normal C++ pointers, which become "dangling pointers" in such cases). <code translate="no">T</code> must be a subclass of <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qobject.html" translate="no">QObject</a>.</p>
